AVAILABLE COMMANDS (Project Manager may ONLY use these for file management; DO NOT use them to create or modify file content):
- join: merge existing files. Usage: {"name": "join", "args": ["output.txt", "input1.txt", "input2.txt"]}
- move: move/rename files. Usage: {"name": "move", "args": ["source", "dest"]}
- copy: copy files. Usage: {"name": "copy", "args": ["source", "dest"]}
- zip: create archive of existing files. Usage: {"name": "zip", "args": ["archive.zip", "source_path"]}
- ftp, sftp: upload existing files. Usage: {"name": "ftp", "args": ["local_file", "ftp_url"]}
- search: list files matching pattern. Usage: {"name": "search", "args": ["pattern", "optional_dir"]}
- insert: copy content from a source file into a target file. Usage: {"name": "insert", "args": ["target.txt", "source.txt", "optional_pattern"]}

You must NOT use echo or any shell command. The only commands you may use are: join, move, copy, zip, ftp, sftp, search, insert. All content creation must be delegated to the leaf generation step (via generate).
